# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects: "from to status". Never change a published URL without a 301 here
# (docs/SEO_AND_SHARING.md). Add one line per moved page, above the catch-alls.
#
# Not here, because they need the real domain and are set in the host's dashboard: www <-> apex and HTTP -> HTTPS.

# The RSS feeds were removed (docs/DECISIONS.md). Cloudflare Pages cannot answer 410 from this file (it allows 200, 301, 302, 303,
# 307 and 308), so every old feed address, and the usual guesses for one, goes to the home page. 302, not 301, so a browser or reader
# does not remember the move if the feeds are ever restored.
/rss.xml            /   302
/news/rss.xml       /   302
/blog/rss.xml       /   302
/vlogs/rss.xml      /   302
/projects/rss.xml   /   302
/repos/rss.xml      /   302
/feed               /   302
/feed.xml           /   302
/rss                /   302
/atom.xml           /   302

# Common guess for the sitemap.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301

# Without the trailing slash the admin would 404.
/admin      /admin/             301

# The subscribe page was removed with the newsletter (docs/DECISIONS.md). Both forms, so neither depends on how Pages treats the trailing slash.
/subscribe  /                   301
/subscribe/ /                   301
